id: pm-web-culw
title: pm-web close-many previews and closes the whole project instead of only open items
description: "POST /api/projects/:projectId/pm/close-many lists its candidates with ['update-many', '--dry-run', '--status', 'open']. On update-many, --status SETS the status instead of filtering rows, and with no other update flags present the dry-run match set silently widened to every item in the project — closed items included, which then fail the individual close with a conflict and are reported as failed rows. The listing now uses --filter-status open, the flag the command actually defines for row selection."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,bulk-ops,http-semantics
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:42:47.146Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T05:08:27.837Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:08:27.837Z",codex-sol,"Resumed regression suite passes against real HTTP, disposable PostgreSQL, and a scratch pm project (4/4). Preserved the interrupted implementation. Linked-test JSON also needed a single-entry array at the SDK dispatch boundary. Explicit persisted-record and bulk membership assertions pin the behavior."
